# Security Baseline

These standards apply to ALL code in this project.

## Authentication

- Use [JWT/Session] for authentication
- Tokens expire after [1 hour]
- Refresh tokens valid for [7 days]

## Authorization

- Check permissions before data access
- Use middleware for route protection
- Never expose sensitive data in responses

## Data Protection

- Hash passwords with bcrypt (cost factor 12+)
- Encrypt sensitive data at rest
- Use parameterized queries only (no string concatenation)
- Sanitize all user input

## OWASP Top 10 Compliance

- Injection: Use parameterized queries and prepared statements
- Broken Auth: Enforce strong password policies, rate-limit login attempts
- XSS: Escape output, use Content-Security-Policy headers
- CSRF: Use anti-CSRF tokens for state-changing operations
- Security Misconfiguration: No default credentials, disable unnecessary features
- Sensitive Data Exposure: Encrypt in transit (TLS) and at rest
- Broken Access Control: Deny by default, validate on server side
